2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] The table emptiness is a formatting bug in `echo_row2`. It omits the trailing pipe, breaking the
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] markdown table parser.
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] • The bug* (`slopfountain.ts`):
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] function echo_row2(...cells:any):void{
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 	const row = cells.map(String).join('|');
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 	markdownBuffer.push("|"+row);  // Missing trailing |
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] }
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] • The fix*:
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] function echo_row2(...cells:any):void{
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 	const row = cells.map(String).join('|');
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 	markdownBuffer.push("|"+row+"|");
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] }
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] Without the trailing `|`, `flattenTables()` calculates `end=0` and slices out all content with
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] `items.slice(1, 0)`, leaving empty cells that render as your empty box skeleton.
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] • The macOS stdin issue*: Both `slopfountain.ts` (via `slopprompt.ts`) and `sloppybot.ts`
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] (via `sloppyutils.ts`) declare readers on `Deno.stdin`. On Unix (macOS), multiple processes reading
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] fd 0 will all receive input; Windows console APIs typically lock stdin to the foreground process
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] only. Run the bot in a separate terminal or disable `readSystem` in the bot when running colocated.
2026-02-03 11:57:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
